    "start": {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's learn order of operations, bodmas, brackets and modulus.\n\nThis lesson uses the methods and question patterns from the Simplification chapter.\n\nWe will keep each step small: understand one rule, see it with numbers, then try a similar question.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "concept_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "concept_1": {
      "id": "concept_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "BODMAS tells us which operation to do first.\n\nIn this chapter the order is:\n\nBrackets → of → Division → Multiplication → Addition → Subtraction.\n\nDo not try to do the whole line at once. Circle the next operation, simplify only that part, then rewrite the shorter expression.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
